 "about_text": "EUKARYOTE is a contemporary art gallery in Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, established in 2018. Taking its name from the biological term for organisms whose cells contain a nucleus, the gallery frames its program around a recurring cycle of artistic evolution, likening it to the metabolism of living systems. It presents artists and artworks engaging with the tension between tangibility and intangibility in contemporary practice. Since opening, EUKARYOTE has regularly participated in art fairs across Japan and abroad, including ART OSAKA, Art Fair Asia Fukuoka, Art Collaboration Kyoto, and international fairs such as ART OnO Seoul, alongside group exhibitions and gallery-weekend events in Tokyo. The gallery represents a roster of primarily Japanese contemporary artists working across painting and other media.",
